sec.p:
scDiffusion-X is a multi-modal latent denoising diffusion probabilistic model for single-cell multi-omics data generation. The architecture has two main components: a multimodal autoencoder and a multimodal denoising network. The multimodal autoencoder encodes each modality from the multi-omics data into a low-dimensional latent space, facilitating diffusion-based learning, and subsequently decodes it back to its original space (Fig. 1a). The multimodal denoising network operates in latent space, progressively refining noisy representations to recover biologically meaningful multi-omics data (Fig. 1b, c). A key innovation of scDiffusion-X is the DCA module, integrated within the multimodal denoising network, to effectively integrate information from different modalities in an interpretable way (Fig. 1d). Additionally, condition labels, such as cell type, tissue, disease state, or experimental condition, are embedded into the time-step representations, allowing scDiffusion-X to generate context-specific multi-omics data.Fig. 1An interpretable deep generative framework for single cell multi-omics data analysis.
a An overview of the scDiffusion-X model. scDiffusion-X is a latent diffusion model that consists of encoders, decoders, coupled with a multimodal denoising network. b The multimodal denoising network. The forward process adds noise to the latent representation in each time step and the reverse process aims to remove noise from a random generated noisy latent representation with the multimodal denoising network parameterized by \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
