				\begin{document}$$\theta$$\end{document}θ. c The architecture of the multimodal denoising network from time t to t-1 where the condition and time step are used as additional inputs. d The dual-cross-attention (DCA) module. This module uses a cross-attention mechanism to integrate information from different modalities. e scDiffusion-X model provides solutions to various downstream tasks.

The gradient-based interpretability approach and DCA can be used to identify the cell-type-specific highly attended genes or peaks. We first identified the genes that were most attended to by peaks within each cell type. There are three DCA module in scDiffusion-X, we take the second DCA module as an example for illustration. We averaged the ATAC-to-RNA attention map across cells within each cell type and then averaged it across the ATAC axis, resulting in a \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
